        description
            Build the CLI's `check`, `explain` and `graph` from @spec.StaticCli; the CLI stays at check, explain,
            graph, story, trace.

            **Why now:** Compiled has no static front end, so nothing yet answers the static cases.

            **Read first:** @spec.StaticCli, @spec.StaticCli.I2 (graph edge names equal the turn record's),
            @spec.Compile, @spec.Diagnostics.

            **Scope added** (the user, 2026-11-11, from
            code:workflow/plans/flow/references/proposals/plan-task-coverage-2026-11-11.md): add cases for StaticCli R6:
            static explain and `explain <release> --since <release>` (rows C02, C03, owed checks), and own lint autofix,
            which orders category keys (C13; @plan.CommandLine.O1, @plan.CommandLine.O5).

            **Read first (added):** @plan.CommandLine.O1, @plan.CommandLine.O5.

            **Slice 6, CLI and close-out (replan, accepted 2026-11-11):** `flow check`, `explain` and `graph` with the
            static cases StaticCli I3, I10 and I11 from `not-yet.ts`, then @task.V3.T15 (the cross-slice audit) and
            @task.V3.T23 (the round-14 adapter leaves the gates). This is the old P3 and P4 close-out, now after every
            core Spec is built. The StaticCli Spec change comes first (C13 lint autofix order; C15 one sentence on
            package instances). No parts are built. Effort 4 (estimate). Read first:
            code:workflow/plans/flow/references/proposals/replan-2026-11-11.md (part 3, "6 CLI and close-out").

            - **May change:** `src/`.
            - **Evidence:** this Task's comments.
            - **False pass:** graph edges named differently from the turn record → caught by the
              graph gate.
            - **Gates:** StaticCli cases; graph gate.
            - **Stops:** public entry-point names.
        acceptance
            - StaticCli cases and the graph gate pass on production.
            - StaticCli R6 has cases for static explain and `--since`; lint autofix orders category keys.
            - Declared: no new runtime code; the matrix rows for `check`, `explain`, `graph` and lint name their static
              cases as the fixture kind, and none is owed.
            - Enabled: the Compile static cases run on every composite's `Compiled`, not on one fixture.
            - Covered: the combination and matrix gates pass over every implemented code, with dated waivers only for
              codes of slices 7 to 10.
            - Guards: production's first-contact reds are recorded and classified, held-out seeds pass, and a sample of
              the model's expectations is read by a different model family (Fable).
        comment     2026-11-10T21:23:15Z
            Owns, in conformance/not-yet.ts, StaticCli I3, I10 and I11 (round-14's CLI loads every fixture before 
            reading its arguments and has no config discovery or project tree); their static cases land before this 
            Task closes. Also owed here: spies for I1 (StaticCli T1), the R10 rules round-14 lacks (unfilled ports, 
            late handler, DuplicatePlacement, VerbMismatch, KeyFieldOptional, ReservedReason, the allowlist grammar), 
            I4 for graph and explain, R7's envelope (version, status, data), and whether desk's UnresolvedHold errors 
            are right. Detail: conformance/STATUS.md, T13 part 2.
